#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid "Monitor &amp; Display"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid "This module allows you to change the various monitor and display settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Changes in this module are stored in <filename>/etc/X11/xorg.conf</filename> "
"and are the main settings that control the refresh rate, resolution, color, "
"power saving, and driver configuration. This module is separated into four "
"sections:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Size, Orientation, &amp; Positioning (see <xref linkend=\"kcmdisplay-size\"/"
">)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid "Color &amp; Gamma (see <xref linkend=\"kcmdisplay-color\"/>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hardware (see <xref linkend=\"kcmdisplay-hw\"/>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid "Power saving (see <xref linkend=\"kcmdisplay-pwrsav\"/>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "Size, Orientation, &amp; Position"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section allows you to configure the <guilabel>Screen size</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Refresh</guilabel>, <guilabel>Monitor Orientation</guilabel>, as "
"well as a <guilabel>Second screen</guilabel> if you have one installed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "Monitor Orientation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "Normal"
msgstr "Normal"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the default setting and the most common setting. This will cause "
"your desktop to be displayed horizontally."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid "Left edge on top"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This setting will allow you to rotate your desktop ninety degrees clockwise, "
"or to the right. Screen resolutions are greater horizontally, so this "
"setting is used mostly for people who write often and need a page to be "
"displayed longer than it would be in the <guilabel>Normal</guilabel> "
"orientation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "Right edge on top"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the same as the previous, <guilabel>Left edge on top</guilabel>, "
"however it rotates your desktop ninety degrees counter-clockwise, or to the "
"left."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "Upsidedown"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option flips your desktop orientation horizontally, making the desktop "
"appear upside down. This is used if you were to mount your monitor upside "
"down from a shelving unit or such. After doing so, selecting this will make "
"your desktop appear correctly and not upside down."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "Second screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "Clone primary screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid "This option puts your desktop on both displays."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "Dual screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option extends your desktop to another screen providing you with double "
"the amount of workspace."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screen size"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lower"
msgstr "Mai bas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "This side of the slider provides a lower resolution."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid "Higher"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "This side of the slider provides a higher resolution."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "Resolution"
msgstr "Resolucion"

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:147 index.docbook:179 index.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid "Dropdown dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dropdown selection allows you to select a proper resolution. Depending "
"on your monitor, you may only have one selection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid "Color &amp; Gamma"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section allows you to configure the color calibration of your display "
"by utilizing a pre-configured setting or by your own custom setting. Unless "
"you are sure about what settings you need, the default color and gamma is "
"usually the best."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "Color calibration image"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid "Gamma controls how your monitor displays colors."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For accurate color reproduction, adjust the gamma correction sliders until "
"the squares blend into the background as much as possible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screen"
msgstr "Ecran"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option allows you to select the screen you would like to configure. You "
"will only have <guilabel>Screen 1</guilabel> as a selection unless you have "
"more than one display."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "Gamma correction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>All</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This slider allows you to control the red, green, and blue colors at one "
"time in unison."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Red</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid "Green"
msgstr "Vèrd"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid "Blue"
msgstr "Blau"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This selection allows you independently change each color setting to your "
"preference."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid "Target gamma"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dropdown dialog allows you to select from various pre-configured "
"settings which are considered an industry standard in some aspects."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hardware"
msgstr "Material"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section allows you to configure hardware and driver settings for your "
"graphics card(s) as well as monitor(s)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid "Administrative access"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to make changes to this section, you will need to press the "
"<guibutton>Administrator Mode</guibutton> button and enter your user "
"password when prompted. You will notice that your <guibutton>Configure...</"
"guibutton> buttons will become available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid "Graphics card"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This subsection will allow you to view your <guilabel>Graphics card</"
"guilabel> and <guilabel>Driver</guilabel> as well as configure this hardware "
"by pressing the <guibutton>Configure...</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Choose Graphics Card</guilabel> Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:252
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this dialog you can select your graphics card and if applicable you will "
"be able to select either a <guilabel>Standard</guilabel> or "
"<guilabel>Proprietary</guilabel> driver solution and select the amount of "
"<guilabel>Video RAM</guilabel> necessary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you choose a graphics card from the list, press the <guibutton>Select</"
"guibutton> button to select and load the card and driver."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Choose Monitor</guilabel> Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:268
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this dialog you can select your monitor as well as your image format. You "
"can attempt to use the <guibutton>Detect Monitor</guibutton> button in order "
"to automatically locate and configure your monitor. If this option doesn't "
"work, you can manually select the monitor from the list. In the "
"<guilabel>Image format</guilabel> dropdown, you can select from "
"<guimenuitem>Standard 4:3</guimenuitem> or <guimenuitem>Widescreen 16:9</"
"guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid "Power saving"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this section you have the option of enabling or disabling power saving "
"for your monitor as well as setting the amount of time in which after it has "
"reached, the monitor will switch off."
msgstr ""

